          "title": "Protein Synthesis and Metabolism Overview",
          "html": "<h2>Week 9: Protein Synthesis and Metabolism Overview</h2>\n<p><strong>What this week covers:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Transcription; the genetic code; translation; mutations and genetic\ndisease; modern DNA technology; viruses</li>\n<li>Overview of metabolism; ATP and energy production; coenzymes in metabolism</li>\n<li>Lab: DNA Extraction</li>\n<li>Required Reading: Smith Ch. 17 (17.6–17.11), Ch. 18 (18.1–18.3)</li>\n</ul>\n<details>\n<summary>Weekly logistics</summary><ul>\n<li>Activity: A37 (17.6–17.11)</li>\n<li>Activity: A38 (18.1–18.3)</li>\n<li>Seed-toxicology lab prep begins this week (advance germination time)</li>\n</ul>\n</details><!-- Week 10 merges what are, on the real Fall calendar, two separate weeks (holiday-shortened Week 10 + Week 11) — Fall is the only term with an 11th week (Thanksgiving). In 10-week Winter/Spring terms, this same final content unit IS Week 10, no merge needed. Keep this card as \"Week 10\" across all terms so the template doesn't have to change term to term. -->"
